// update.bif — Arty Z7 UPDATE BOOT.BIN (Case B), QSPI offset 0x700000
//
// The only region the updater may write. This image is what gets served over
// TFTP as update.bin and programmed into the slot; it is never flashed directly
// in the field, only by the updater that verified it twice.
//
// Identical structure to golden.bif, and two of the three partitions are the
// SAME FILES:
//
//   fsbl.elf      the same hooked FSBL, byte for byte. Not an oversight and not
//                 laziness -- it is the design. One arbiter binary means the
//                 golden and update boots cannot disagree about the rules, and
//                 it removes the whole class of bug where a fix lands in one
//                 image and not the other. It decides its role at runtime from
//                 multiboot_slot_index().
//
//   blinkctl_v2   VERSION 0x0002_0001, 4 Hz. THE ONLY DELIBERATE DIFFERENCE
//                 from golden, and the one you can see from across the room.
//                 Same RTL, two generic values.
//
//   updater.elf   the same updater binary. Here it comes up in its UPDATE role:
//                 arm the watchdog, prove the payload's heartbeat is moving,
//                 then clear boot_attempts -- the commit. Failing to reach that
//                 commit is what eventually returns the board to golden.
//
// For fault-campaign item F7, build a deliberately broken v2 by compiling the
// updater with -DUPDATER_FAULT_HANG=1 and rebuilding this image. It will come
// up, prove healthy, and then hang before committing; the watchdog resets it,
// the arbiter counts 1 -> 2 -> 3, and at BOOT_ATTEMPTS_MAX the board falls back
// to golden reporting the failure. That path is the entire safety argument of
// Case B and it is not proven until it has been watched.
//
// NOT compressed, same reasoning as golden.bif -- 4.08 MB into an 8.94 MB slot,
// 45.7% used.

the_ROM_image:
{
  [bootloader] build/vitis_ws/ps_plat/zynq_fsbl/fsbl.elf
  build/boot/blinkctl_v2.bit
  build/vitis_ws/updater/Debug/updater.elf
}
